    {
      "value": "remorac is a Python re-imagining of Remora (ML-syntax), not the Kennedy Haskell implementation; int is i32-only, so u64/Goldilocks are emulated byte-wise",
      "provenance": "specified"
    },
    {
      "value": "No wall-clock builtin exists in the dialect; timing protocol values are null/unknown, not measured",
      "provenance": "specified"
    },
    {
      "value": "iota requires a compile-time constant shape in remorac; stream sizes are fixed per program",
      "provenance": "specified"
    },
    {
      "value": "remorac's whole-program typechecker rejects the monolithic program (binary map over indexing functions; first-class (==); 9-element array results); the five split programs are the executed artifacts",
